  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Three zones – recover goal-side",
  "description": "An area of about 21 × 12 metres is split into three equal zones with cones. Each zone has one attacker (blue) and one defender (red). Two attackers with a ball start behind the first zone and enter it, making it 3v1.\n\nThe attackers must get through all three zones. When they enter the next zone, everyone – attackers and defenders – may follow. A defender who has been beaten must therefore race back and get goal-side in the next zone, so the overload shrinks.\n\nIf the defenders win the ball they score by playing it out behind the start line, and the attackers try to win it back. Swap roles after a while, and play rounds of about three minutes with mobility work in between. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Defenders: if you are beaten, run back on the shortest line towards the goal, not towards the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Get between the ball and the goal before you try to win the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Press the ball carrier outwards, away from the middle."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Attackers: use the overload quickly, before the defenders get back."
    }
  ],
